Quasar-authored. Issue #1663: a PyroWave stop could hang the agent forever on NVIDIA.

The pyrowaveenc element hands PyroWave the session's shared VkDevice (borrowed:
Granite's Context has owned_device = false). Granite still called vkDeviceWaitIdle
on it, in Device::wait_idle_nolock (device destroy, and init_frame_contexts at
create) holding only the one queue lock it is given, and again in
Context::destroy_device with no lock at all. vkDeviceWaitIdle needs every queue of
the device externally synchronised; the compositor and the Vulkan video encoder keep
submitting on that device while PyroWave is torn down, and NVIDIA 615.78.08 then
waited forever with the GPU idle.

On a borrowed device Granite now waits only for its own submissions: every one is
recorded in a frame (a per-queue timeline value, or a fence without timeline
semaphores), so waiting each frame covers all queues Granite submits to before it
frees anything. The owned-device path is unchanged. Applied to Granite at
GRANITE_REF by deploy/Dockerfile.vulkan; re-apply on every PyroWave/Granite bump.

diff --git a/vulkan/context.cpp b/vulkan/context.cpp
index ad9e9c8b..85856ecb 100644
--- a/vulkan/context.cpp
+++ b/vulkan/context.cpp
@@ -294,7 +294,9 @@ bool Context::init_device_from_instance(VkInstance instance_, VkPhysicalDevice g
 
 void Context::destroy_device()
 {
-	if (device != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
+	// A borrowed device has other users submitting on its queues without our lock;
+	// Device::~Device already waited for Granite's own work.
+	if (owned_device && device != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
 		device_table.vkDeviceWaitIdle(device);
 
 #if defined(ANDROID) && defined(HAVE_SWAPPY)
diff --git a/vulkan/context.hpp b/vulkan/context.hpp
index b36a7dc7..ce16cafc 100644
--- a/vulkan/context.hpp
+++ b/vulkan/context.hpp
@@ -355,6 +355,11 @@ public:
 		owned_device = false;
 	}
 
+	bool owns_device() const
+	{
+		return owned_device;
+	}
+
 	const DeviceFeatures &get_enabled_device_features() const
 	{
 		return ext;
diff --git a/vulkan/device.cpp b/vulkan/device.cpp
index ee4298ce..5ca62ece 100644
--- a/vulkan/device.cpp
+++ b/vulkan/device.cpp
@@ -2655,7 +2655,16 @@ void Device::wait_idle_nolock()
 	if (!per_frame.empty())
 		end_frame_nolock();
 
-	if (device != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
+	if (device != VK_NULL_HANDLE && ctx && !ctx->owns_device())
+	{
+		// Borrowed device: other users submit on its queues without our queue lock, so
+		// vkDeviceWaitIdle would be externally unsynchronised. Every Granite submission is
+		// tracked by a frame (timeline value or fence), so waiting the frames covers our own work.
+		for (auto &frame : per_frame)
+			if (!frame->wait(UINT64_MAX))
+				LOGE("Waiting for own submissions on a borrowed device failed.\n");
+	}
+	else if (device != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
 	{
 		if (queue_lock_callback)
 			queue_lock_callback();
